   2043: ⟪ 921 characters skipped ⟫e fish. The juvenlile\u2019s diet is unknown. It has appeared in reasonable numbers (~1% by no.) in KZN commercial ski-boat catches at times, much less common in recreational ski-boat catches; small (< 1%) contribution to semi-industrial linefish catches in southern MOZ. It is seldom taken by spearfishermen due to its preference for deeper water.", "biology": "The reproductive style of Yellowfin Emperor is unknown. Ripe fish have been seen in Oct and Jan in Kenya. Their breeding/spawning locality is unknown in SA; recorded on Seychelles Bank and in Kenyan waters. Their age and length at maturity is also unknown. The maximum recorded age is also unknown. The maximum recorded weight is 8,8 kg and the maximum recorded length is 600 mm TL.", "citation": "ST Fennessy, BQ Mann In: Mann BQ. (Ed). Southern African Marine Linefish Species Profiles. Special Publication, Oceanographic Research Institute, Durban 9: 179-180, FAO Fisheries Synopsis No. 125, Volume 9 EMPEROR FISHES AND LARGE-EYE BREAMS OF THE WORLD"}',
