   2091    '{"other_names": "", "meristics": "Dorsal spines: 12; Dorsal soft rays: 10; Anal spines: 3; Anal soft rays: 8.", "appearance": "T he Englishman is a deep-bodied fish with a steep head profile and a slightly concave snout. Silvery pink in colour with blue dots on the upper body scales. It has 4 vertical red crossbars on body and a fifth through the eye. Red colour is variable and becomes paler after death.", "about": "Englishman are endemic to southern Africa stretching from southern MOZ to Algoa Bay with the main stock assumed to be found between southern MOZ and the former Transkei. Based on limited tagging data, this species appears to be highly resident. Adults inhabit offshore reefs between 20-120 m while juveniles are observed on shallow subtidal reefs between 10-30 m in the Pondoland region of the EC. Adults eat benthic crustaceans and mollusks; the juvenile\u2019s diet is unknown. Englishman are important in the KZN commercial and recreational ski-boat fishery, particularly on the KZN south coast and are occasionally taken by competitive spearfishers. Following completion of the stock assessment in 2004 and the implementation of a minimum size limit in 2005 (40 cm TL), catch and effort for this species should be carefully monitored.", "biology": "Reproductive style: Englishman are assumed to be protogynous hermaphrodite (born female and changes sex to male). Breeding/spawning season: Limited data but appears to have an extended spawning season during winter and spring. Breeding/spawning locality: Unknown, limited spawning recorded in KZN. Age at maturity: Based on the approximate length at maturity of 40 cm TL, the corresponding age would be about 7 years. Length at maturity: estimated size at maturity at 40 cm TL. Fish sampled with active gonads ranged in length from 315-600 mm FL. Maximum recorded age: 17 years; male; KZN. Maximum recorded weight: 7 kg (SADSAA). Maximum recorded length: 80 cm TL.", "citation": "BQ Mann, PA Garratt In: Mann BQ. (Ed). Southern African Marine Linefish Species Profiles. Special Publication, Oceanographic Research Institute, Durban 9: 179-180, ORI Fact Sheet For more information: http://speciesstatus.sanbi.org/assessment/last-assessment/1022/"}',

