   2547: ⟪ 850 characters skipped ⟫n in spring. Adults >90 cm are found throughout distributional range, over sandy and rocky substrata to depths of 150 m. Juveniles occupy sandy and rocky substrata to depths of 100 m, early juveniles <50 cm in SE Cape, while sub-adults 50-85 cm are mainly found in the SW Cape. Adults feed on sardines (which are considered depleted), mackerel and massbanker while juveniles on shrimps and later anchovies. Geelbek are an important catch of the boat-based commercial and recreational linefishery. Catches per area are seasonal as adult fish undertake an annual spawning migration to KZN. They are also taken as bycatch by the inshore demersal trawl fishery. Despite the cut in commercial fishing effort and the decrease in recreational bag limits, the standardised CPUE does not indicate much of an improvement. Fishing concentrated on spawning adults needs to be regulated to improve this stock. The current high level of shark predation on adults hooked in these spawning aggregations along the KZN coast is further exacerbating the problem.", "biology": "Reproductive style: Gonochorist (separate sexes). Breeding/spawning season: Aug-Nov with peak in Sep-Oct. Breeding/spawning locality: In KZN w
   2548    '[{"measure": "FL", "reference": "Visboekie", "coefficient": 8.42e-06, "exponent": 3.01, "formula_type": "power-mm", "result_unit": "g"}]'

