  10778    'Over exploited, 25-40% of pristine',
  10779: ⟪ 628 characters skipped ⟫ica they are found from Saldanha Bay in WC to Maputo in MOZ. They are migrants. Adults migrate from juvenile nursery areas in EC and WC to breed in warmer KZN waters. They remain in the inshore zone (<15 m) and there is little evidence of a return migration to the Cape, although some of the largest specimens have been caught in Cape waters. Adults inhabit subtidal gullies and over shallow rocky reefs, largely confined to the surf-zone. Juveniles are found in tidal rockpools, sandy littoral, shallow reefs and estuaries in the EC and WC. Very small juveniles (27-29 mm SL) have been recorded at the sea surface about 4km offshore on the KZN south coast during Aug being driven south to juvenile nursery areas by strong NE winds. Adults are herbivorous feeding mainly on red algae but also occasionally on hydrozoans and bivalve mollusks. They are an abundant and important grazer in the inshore marine environment. Juveniles <3 cm feed mainly on planktonic organisms such as copepods (crabs, shrimps, and prawns) but with growth they change to become herbivorous with an associated change in dentition. Strepies are harvested almost exclusively by shore anglers and subsistence shore fishers throughout their distribution and is the second most important species by number (after Elf /shad) caught along the KZN and EC coast. They are used for both food and bait.", "biology": "Reproductive style: Protandrous hermaphrodite (changes sex from male to hermaphrodite). Breeding/spawning season: Winter and spring (Apr-Sep), peaking from Jun-Aug in KZN.  Peak numbers of eggs in plankton samples have been recorded on the KZN south coast from Apr-Aug. Breeding/spawning locality: Over shallow (<15 m) subtidal reefs along the KZN coast. Some spawning has also been recorded in EC waters. Age at maturity: Combined sexes: 1.5 years; KZN. Length at maturity: Males: 140-150 mm FL; Females: 160-170 mm FL; KZN. Combined sexes: 145 mm FL; KZN. Maximum recorded age: 6 years; female; KZN. Maximum recorded weight: 0.7 kg; (SASAA). There are reports of this species reaching a maximum weight of 2 kg, but this is considered unlikely in SA waters. Maximum recorded length: 30 cm TL. Also reports of reaching a maximum length of 45 cm TL but this is considered unlikely in SA waters.", "citation": "BQ Mann, SW Dunlop In: Mann BQ. (Ed). Southern African Marine Linefish Species Profiles. Special Publication, Oceanographic Research Institute, Durban 9: 179-180 FishBase, Two Oceans Aquarium For more information: http://speciesstatus.sanbi.org/assessment/last-assessment/1007/"}',
